    "message": "Let generated Scenarios shorter than four days take outages and absences\n\nA water outage or a staff absence needs operational_events_v1, which a\nScenario got only when it planned an operational event. Generated\nScenarios plan their first supply delivery on day 4, so shorter ones\nrejected both interventions before the Branch existed (#65).\n\nGenerated Scenarios now set model_configs.operational_events.enabled,\nand WorldState.from_scenario creates the state for it as it does for\nplanned events. The state check requires the state whenever the config\nasks for it. Scenarios saved without the config keep running without\nthe state, so their Checkpoints still restore.\n\nThe pinned generated_small run gets new Scenario and final-state\nhashes; its realized events are unchanged. The outcome tests for the\noutage and the absence now fork the shared six-hour main line instead\nof building a four-day Scenario.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
